<section xml:id="confidence-intervals-for-a-population-proportion">
  <title>Inference for One Proportion Part 1</title>

  <objectives>
    <ol marker="1)">
      <li><p>Distinguish a point estimate from an interval estimate of a population proportion.</p></li>
      <li><p>Explain the meaning of a confidence interval, confidence level, and margin of error.</p></li>
      <li><p>Check the conditions for a one-proportion z-interval.</p></li>
      <li><p>Find a normal critical value and construct a confidence interval by calculation and in R.</p></li>
      <li><p>Interpret an interval in context and assess whether a proposed population proportion is compatible with it.</p></li>
      <li><p>Explain how confidence level and sample size affect precision, and distinguish one-sided bounds from two-sided intervals.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </objectives>

